Move the news spool directory from /var/lib/gentoo/news to
/var/lib/macaroni/news. The old path is only ever touched by the
bundled news module (NEWS_DIR below) and by the ebuild that creates
the directory; nothing else in the Macaroni OS stack reads it (for
example, macaronictl has no news support at all). Ownership and
group-writability semantics are unchanged. Requested on
macaroni-os/kit-fixups#523, part of macaroni-os/mark-issues#857.
--- a/modules/news.eselect
+++ b/modules/news.eselect
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 DESCRIPTION="Read Gentoo (\"GLEP 42\") news items"
 MAINTAINER="ulm@gentoo.org"
 
-NEWS_DIR="/var/lib/gentoo/news"
+NEWS_DIR="/var/lib/macaroni/news"
 
 # read list of news items
 # list of parameters may contain "unread" or "read"
